    "message": {
     "content": "**Yes, you should accept it.** This is an exceptional outcome and a major win.\n\nGetting a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus** at Google L6 without a formal competing counteroffer is rare. They effectively converted your unvested Meta RSUs into guaranteed, upfront cash while keeping the $1.08M equity intact and matching your base salary.\n\n---\n\n### The Updated Numbers\n\nAssuming Google\u2019s standard front-loaded vesting (typically 38%/32%/20%/10% or 33%/33%/22%/12%):\n\n| Component | Year 1 | Year 2 |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Bonus (20% target)** | $48,000 | $48,000 |\n| **Sign-On Bonus** | $200,000 | $0 |\n| **Equity Vest (Initial Grant)** | ~$356,000 \u2013 $410,000 | ~$345,000 \u2013 $356,000 |\n| **Refreshers (Est.)** | $0 | + ~$25,000 \u2013 $40,000 |\n| **Total Compensation** | **~$844,000 \u2013 $898,000** | **~$658,000 \u2013 $684,000** |\n\n### Why This Is a Home Run\n\n1. **Massive 2-Year Upside:** Over your first two years at Google, you will clear roughly **~$1.5M to ~$1.58M**, compared to **~$1.05M** if you stayed at Meta\u2014a net gain of roughly **+$450,000 to +$500,000**.\n2. **De-risked Equity:** Cash in hand via the sign-on bonus carries zero market volatility risk compared to holding Meta stock for the next 12 months.\n3. **No Remaining Leverage:** When Google bumps base and adds a $200k sign-on bonus stating it is their \"best and final,\" they mean it. Pushing further without a competing written offer risks burning goodwill with your hiring manager.\n\n---\n\n### Checklist Before Signing\n\nBefore you put pen to paper, confirm these final operational details with your recruiter:\n\n1. **Sign-On Payout & Clawback Terms:** Confirm that the $200k is paid out in your first 1\u20132 paychecks as a lump sum (standard at Google) and verify the clawback duration (typically 12 months prorated).\n2. **Meta Bonus Timing vs. Start Date:** Time your Google start date so you do not forfeit your upcoming Meta annual bonus (usually paid out in March). If you have to forfeit it, ask Google if your start date can be pushed after payout day.\n3. **Vest Schedule & Frequency:** Confirm whether the $1.08M grant vests monthly (standard after month 1) on the 38/32/20/10 or 33/33/22/12 schedule.\n\nUnless you strongly dislike the specific Google team or project scope compared to your current Meta work, **this is an offer you should sign.**",
